@page "/waterfall"

<PageTitle>Waterfall · RioCharts for Blazor and .NET</PageTitle>

<h1>Waterfall</h1>
<p class="lead">
    A waterfall shows how a start value becomes an end value: a month's result from revenue through costs, or a budget through its
    changes. Each change is a bar floating from the running total before it to the one after, and totals stand on zero.
</p>

<Example Title="From revenue to result" Code="@ResultCode">
    <Description>
        <p>
            Give <code>WaterfallSeries</code> the changes as <code>YValue</code> and mark the totals with <code>IsTotal</code>. A total shows the
            running total so far, so its own value is ignored (it can be null); a subtotal in between keeps the total running. Rises are
            green and falls red (<code>--rio-positive</code> and <code>--rio-negative</code>), totals take the series color, and thin lines
            carry each bar's end over to the next. The tooltip shows the change and the running total after it.
        </p>
    </Description>
    <ChildContent>
        <RioChart TItem="Step" Items="Result" YAxis="Keur" Height="280">
            <WaterfallSeries Name="Result" XValue="s => s.Name" YValue="s => s.Amount" IsTotal="s => s.IsTotal" DataLabels="true" />
        </RioChart>
    </ChildContent>
</Example>

<Example Title="A start value and own colors" Code="@BalanceCode">
    <Description>
        <p>
            The first bar is a change from zero, so an opening balance rises like any other. <code>ColorValue</code> gives it a color of its
            own; here the series color, like the closing total. Bars with their own color keep it in the tooltip.
        </p>
    </Description>
    <ChildContent>
        <RioChart TItem="Step" Items="Balance" YAxis="Keur" Height="260">
            <WaterfallSeries Name="Cash" XValue="s => s.Name" YValue="s => s.Amount" IsTotal="s => s.IsTotal"
                             ColorValue="@(s => s.Name == "Opening" ? "--rio-series-1" : null)" />
        </RioChart>
    </ChildContent>
</Example>

<Example Title="Down the page" Code="@HorizontalCode">
    <Description>
        <p>
            With <code>Horizontal="true"</code> on the chart, the steps run down the side, first on top, and each bar floats left or right
            from the running total. It reads like a statement, and long step names have room.
        </p>
    </Description>
    <ChildContent>
        <RioChart TItem="Step" Items="Result" YAxis="Keur" Height="300" Horizontal="true">
            <WaterfallSeries Name="Result" XValue="s => s.Name" YValue="s => s.Amount" IsTotal="s => s.IsTotal" DataLabels="true" />
        </RioChart>
    </ChildContent>
</Example>

<h2>In JSON definitions</h2>
<p>
    <code>"type": "waterfall"</code> (also <code>"bridge"</code>) with a category <code>x</code>, the changes as <code>y</code>, and
    <code>"total"</code>: the field that marks total rows (<code>true</code>, <code>yes</code> or <code>1</code>). <code>"horizontal": true</code>
    runs the steps down the rows.
</p>

@code {
    private sealed record Step(string Name, double? Amount, bool IsTotal = false);

    private static readonly AxisOptions Keur = new() { Title = "k€" };

    private static readonly Step[] Result =
    [
        new("Revenue", 420), new("Cost of sales", -180), new("Gross profit", null, true),
        new("Salaries", -120), new("Marketing", -45), new("Other income", 15), new("Result", null, true),
    ];

    private static readonly Step[] Balance =
    [
        new("Opening", 250), new("Customers", 310), new("Suppliers", -190), new("Payroll", -140),
        new("Tax", -35), new("Loan", 60), new("Closing", null, true),
    ];

    private const string ResultCode = """
        <RioChart TItem="Step" Items="steps">
            <WaterfallSeries Name="Result" XValue="s => s.Name" YValue="s => s.Amount"
                             IsTotal="s => s.IsTotal" DataLabels="true" />
        </RioChart>

        @code {
            record Step(string Name, double? Amount, bool IsTotal = false);

            Step[] steps =
            [
                new("Revenue", 420), new("Cost of sales", -180), new("Gross profit", null, true),
                new("Salaries", -120), new("Marketing", -45), new("Other income", 15), new("Result", null, true),
            ];
        }
        """;

    private const string BalanceCode = """
        <RioChart TItem="Step" Items="steps">
            <WaterfallSeries Name="Cash" XValue="s => s.Name" YValue="s => s.Amount" IsTotal="s => s.IsTotal"
                             ColorValue="@(s => s.Name == "Opening" ? "--rio-series-1" : null)" />
        </RioChart>
        """;

    private const string HorizontalCode = """
        <RioChart TItem="Step" Items="steps" Horizontal="true">
            <WaterfallSeries Name="Result" XValue="s => s.Name" YValue="s => s.Amount"
                             IsTotal="s => s.IsTotal" DataLabels="true" />
        </RioChart>
        """;
}
